{"id":"2L","title":"Confession and Repentance of Sins","part":{"n":2,"title":"Relationship to God"},"url":"/law/02-relationship-to-god/2l","entries":[{"id":"2L.1","text":"Repentance commanded to all by God.","refs":[{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":14,"verses":"6"},{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":18,"verses":"30,32"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":3,"verses":"2"},{"book":"Mark","chapter":6,"verses":"12"},{"book":"Acts","chapter":17,"verses":"30"}],"citation":"Ezek. 14:6; Ezek. 18:30, 32; Matt. 3:2; Mark 6:12; Acts 17:30."},{"id":"2L.2","text":"Repentance commanded by Christ.","refs":[{"book":"Matthew","chapter":4,"verses":"17"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":9,"verses":"13"},{"book":"Mark","chapter":1,"verses":"15"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":13,"verses":"3,5"},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":2,"verses":"5,16"},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":3,"verses":"3"}],"citation":"Matt. 4:17; Matt. 9:13; Mark 1:15; Luke 13:3, 5; Rev. 2:5, 16; Rev. 3:3."},{"id":"2L.3","text":"God requires confessing of sins to Him (not to men).","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":5,"verses":"5-6"},{"book":"Hosea","chapter":5,"verses":"15"}],"citation":"Lev. 5:5-6; Hosea 5:15."},{"id":"2L.4","text":"Confession of sins is regarded by God through deliverance. 1. Sam. 12:10-11;","refs":[{"book":"Job","chapter":33,"verses":"27-29"}],"citation":"Job. 33:27-29."},{"id":"2L.5","text":"Confession and repentance necessary to pardon sin and for God to release us from His chastisements and punishments.","refs":[{"book":"1 Kings","chapter":8,"verses":"35-39"},{"book":"Acts","chapter":2,"verses":"38"},{"book":"Acts","chapter":3,"verses":"19"},{"book":"Acts","chapter":8,"verses":"22"},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":3,"verses":"19"}],"citation":"1 Kings 8:35-39; Acts 2:38; Acts 3:19; Acts 8:22; Rev. 3:19."},{"id":"2L.6","text":"We are exhorted to acknowledge our transgressions and iniquity and confess them to God.","refs":[{"book":"Joshua","chapter":7,"verses":"19"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":32,"verses":"5"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":51,"verses":"3"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":3,"verses":"13"},{"book":"1 John","chapter":1,"verses":"9"}],"citation":"Josh. 7:19; Psa. 32:5; Psa. 51:3; Jer. 3:13; 1 John 1:9."},{"id":"2L.7","text":"True repentance is evidenced by one's fruits.","refs":[{"book":"Daniel","chapter":4,"verses":"27"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":3,"verses":"8"},{"book":"Acts","chapter":26,"verses":"20"}],"citation":"Dan. 4:27; Matt. 3:8; Acts 26:20."},{"id":"2L.8","text":"He who covers his sins will not prosper, but whoever confesses and forsakes them will have mercy.","refs":[{"book":"Psalms","chapter":32,"verses":"5"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":28,"verses":"13"}],"citation":"Psa. 32:5; Prov. 28:13."},{"id":"2L.9","text":"The word of God to be read to aid in repentance.","refs":[{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":36,"verses":"6-7"}],"citation":"Jer. 36:6-7"},{"id":"2L.10","text":"Confession and supplication to God required before God will release a nation from enemy infliction or captivity.","refs":[{"book":"1 Kings","chapter":8,"verses":"33-34"},{"book":"Nehemiah","chapter":1,"verses":"3-7"}],"citation":"1 Kings 8:33-34; Neh. 1:3-7."},{"id":"2L.11","text":"In prayer make repentance to God that He may blot out your transgressions.","refs":[{"book":"Psalms","chapter":51,"verses":"1"}],"citation":"Psa. 51:1."},{"id":"2L.12","text":"Confessing of iniquities and turning from them required before God will give mercy and restore His blessings to a people.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":26,"verses":"40-42"},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":7,"verses":"13-14"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":55,"verses":"7"},{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":18,"verses":"21,27-28"}],"citation":"Lev. 26:40-42; 2 Chron. 7:13-14; Isa. 55:7; Ezek. 18:21, 27-28."},{"id":"2L.13","text":"We should repent of any uncleanness, fornication, and lasciviousness committed.","refs":[{"book":"2 Corinthians","chapter":12,"verses":"21"}],"citation":"2 Cor. 12:21."},{"id":"2L.14","text":"Unless you repent you will perish.","refs":[{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":33,"verses":"14"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":13,"verses":"1-5"}],"citation":"Ezek. 33:14; Luke 13:1-5."}]}